{#
/**
 * @file
 * The site terms at /terms (23-26, ONB-05, D-25).
 *
 * The words are 23-UI-SPEC section 9, word for word: the intro, six h2
 * sections, then the version line. The h1 "Site Terms" is the route title,
 * which Open Social's title block prints, so this template has none.
 *
 * This is a draft that a lawyer reviews before the first real pilot (23-23).
 * When you change any words here, also change
 * SiteTermsController::TERMS_CHANGED to the day of the change; the version
 * line is generated from it, and SiteTermsTest fails until both move
 * together.
 *
 * Variables:
 * - site_name: The community's name (system.site). Autoescaped; site
 *   managers can edit it, so never add a raw-output filter here.
 * - version_date: TERMS_CHANGED, formatted for display ("November 8, 2026").
 * - keeps_wallet_address: TRUE when the optional Web3 stack is on, so members
 *   can connect a wallet and the site stores its public address. Both
 *   sentences are whole, so each translates on its own.
 */
#}
<div class="localnodes-site-terms">
  <p>{% trans %}These are the rules for using {{ site_name }}'s site. They apply to everyone with an account.{% endtrans %}</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-who">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-who">{% trans %}Who runs this site{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <p>{% trans %}{{ site_name }} is run by its organizers. LocalNodes hosts the site.{% endtrans %}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-share">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-share">{% trans %}What you can share{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <p>{% trans %}Share only what you have the right to share: your own words, openly licensed work, or work you have permission to use. When you import files or web pages, you confirm you have that right.{% endtrans %}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-takedown">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-takedown">{% trans %}Taking content down{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <p>{% trans %}If someone tells us a page shouldn't be here, the organizers or the host can unpublish it. Use "Report a problem with this page" on any imported page.{% endtrans %}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-ai">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-ai">{% trans %}The AI assistant{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <p>{% trans %}The AI assistant and the AI overview write answers from pages on this site. They can be wrong. Check the sources they show.{% endtrans %}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-data">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-data">{% trans %}Your personal data{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <ul>
      {% if keeps_wallet_address %}
        <li>{% trans %}What this site keeps: your account name, email address and password record, what you post or upload, and the public address of any wallet you connect.{% endtrans %}</li>
      {% else %}
        <li>{% trans %}What this site keeps: your account name, email address and password record, and what you post or upload.{% endtrans %}</li>
      {% endif %}
      <li>{% trans %}Who can see it: organizers and site managers can see your account details. Other members can't see your email unless you choose to show it on your profile. Posts follow their chosen audience; site managers and administrators can also read private-group records. People with access to the host's servers or hosting accounts, and tools using those accounts, can reach them too.{% endtrans %}</li>
      <li>{% trans %}The AI assistant: to prepare pages for search, this site sends the text of topics, events, posts and comments, and text from their attached files, to its AI service when they are saved. That includes private groups' pages, even if nobody asks the assistant anything. The search index itself is kept with this site's other data. When you ask the assistant something, your question, the passages used and your recent conversation are sent to the same service. When the AI overview summarizes a search, your search words and the passages used are sent. The service may keep requests and answers for a time to check for abuse. Its rules for this site's account, including whether it may use them to improve its products, are being confirmed.{% endtrans %}</li>
      <li>{% trans %}Leaving: ask the site's organizers or <a href="mailto:hello@localnodes.xyz">hello@localnodes.xyz</a> about closing your account or removing records; closing an account does not itself erase this community's records, recovery copies or AI-service logs. The host can also make a copy of the whole site, including every member's account and private pages, so the community can move it elsewhere. If this site was a three-month pilot that doesn't continue, it stays unchanged for 30 days, and the organizers get at least seven days' written notice before it is removed. Removing the site deletes its pages, files and search data; backup copies and the AI service's logs are deleted on their own schedules, not at once.{% endtrans %}</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="localnodes-terms-changes">
    <h2 id="localnodes-terms-changes">{% trans %}Changes{% endtrans %}</h2>
    <p>{% trans %}If these terms change, the date on this page changes and the organizers will tell you.{% endtrans %}</p>
  </section>

  <p class="localnodes-site-terms__version">{% trans %}Draft for review, {{ version_date }}{% endtrans %}</p>
</div>
